    "referencia": "## 1. Swiss Pulse — Josef Müller-Brockmann\n\n**Mood:** Clinical, precise | **Best for:** SaaS dashboards, developer tools, APIs, metrics\n\n```yaml\nname: Swiss Pulse\ncolors:\n  primary: \"#1a1a1a\"\n  on-primary: \"#ffffff\"\n  accent: \"#0066FF\"\ntypography:\n  headline:\n    fontFamily: Helvetica Neue\n    fontSize: 5rem\n    fontWeight: 700\n  label:\n    fontFamily: Inter\n    fontSize: 0.875rem\n    fontWeight: 400\n  stat:\n    fontFamily: Helvetica Neue\n    fontSize: 7rem\n    fontWeight: 700\nrounded:\n  none: 0px\n  sm: 2px\nspacing:\n  sm: 8px\n  md: 16px\n  lg: 32px\nmotion:\n  energy: high\n  easing:\n    entry: \"expo.out\"\n    exit: \"power4.in\"\n    ambient: \"none\"\n  duration:\n    entrance: 0.4\n    hold: 1.5\n    transition: 0.6\n  atmosphere:\n    - grid-lines\n    - registration-marks\n  transition: cinematic-zoom\n```\n\nGrid-locked compositions. Every element snaps to an invisible 12-column grid. Numbers dominate the frame at 80–120px. Animated counters count up from 0. Hard cuts, no decorative transitions. Nothing floats."
